WEBVTT

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.220
The cognition particle emissions increased!

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.890
Are you sure they're coming from inside the house?

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:49.100
Particles <i>have </i>been known to be carried
on the wind from far-away crime scenes.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.720
But as far as I can tell, there's no
indication of a separate murder elsewhere...

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.220
...so they must be.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.600
Is my intent to kill being detected, too?

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:01.600
Feeling hatred or wanting to kill someone,

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.180
however strongly, shouldn't
register on the Wakumusubi.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.520
Freeze! Hands up!

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.930
Put the drill on the floor!

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.140
Obey! We <i>will </i>shoot!

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.850
Put the drill down <i>now</i>!

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:16.430
Just get on your knees!

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.680
We said don't move! We're gonna shoot!

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.890
Shit!

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:22.600
Secured!

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.020
He's not bleeding.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.770
This head wound is old!

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.180
Suspect captured. No one else found.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.810
This is...

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.390
Oonuki Yuji! It's not the Perforator!

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.060
Hey! Are you okay?

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.470
Dammit! What the hell is going on?

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.470
The Perforator took Hondomachi captive and fled!

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.390
How did he pull this off?!

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:27.970
To sum it up, the Perforator had
a hole drilled through his own head.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.890
Not only did he survive,

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.470
but he's been drilling
the same kind of hole in others.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:40.890
When the case is finished, make sure to leave our house, okay?

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.140
Who're you?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.680
Oh, of course I'll leave.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:52.020
As soon as I catch the bad guy.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.220
You won't escape!

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.350
That doesn't fit.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:29.350
It doesn't line up with the structure of this world.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.310
But, there's a reason.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:34.020
Though I guess he did escape...

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.770
What the hell do <i>you </i>want?
Have we met somewhere before?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:00.930
It's John Walker!

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:05.180
Everyone but Togo and Kokufu,
shift all analysis to John Walker.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.220
Draw out whatever information you can.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.600
Yes, sir!

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.520
Hey! Sounds like you're neglecting
the search for Hondomachi!

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.640
It's a temporary reallocation
of the unit's resources.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.520
We haven't abandoned the search.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:19.350
Why?

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.640
It's John Walker, Mr. Matsuoka.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:24.140
The Perforator had contact with John Walker.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:28.600
Shit! I wish you'd at least put a
goddamn GPS on the Wakumusubi!

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.350
I...

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.350
...cannot do that.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:37.020
It may undermine the secrecy of the device.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.600
Chief Hayaseura.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:44.310
Chief, this all happened because
you don't think enough of us!

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:49.220
On the contrary. I think very
highly of the field analysts' work.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:53.850
I ain't talkin' about our work!
I'm talking about our lives!

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:58.180
You should have permitted us
field officers to carry a pistol!

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:01.720
I've been telling you that for months!

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:07.390
Among police organizations, Kura and the Wellside already receive special treatment.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:12.930
And so it's not that your requisition
has been rejected. It just takes time.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:19.270
For now, let's expend every effort to find
Ms. Hondomachi and arrest the suspect.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.930
No shit!

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.600
Dammit!

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:31.140
Although I'm apparently not the fighting type,

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:35.060
it appears I <i>will </i>fight when I have to.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:39.100
Are you... my enemy?

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.680
Over... already?

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.100
Well, let's just say I'm OP and go with it.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.560
Victory!

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.930
Now then.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.680
Are you awake?

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:29.060
I prepared several hideouts
in addition to my residence.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.140
Better safe than sorry, as they say.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:35.970
Have you been confining the
people you've kidnapped here, too?

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.140
Why not kill them right away?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:41.470
Because I have a lot on my mind, you see.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.390
Hey.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:47.270
What is this device?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:55.970
Listen, I'm about to drill a
hole in your head like mine.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:59.560
But few have been able to
answer my questions after that.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.680
So I'd like you to answer me now.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:06.180
"Few"? Don't they all die immediately?

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:10.390
No one dies immediately. They linger for a while.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:14.810
The guy I left in my house is fine for now, too.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:18.350
Unless he's been shot in my place, that is.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:24.850
You drilled a whole in your head yourself?
Then you did it to others?

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:27.890
What, are you making a club?

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:32.520
First wind comes in this hole,
then it goes out of the other,

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:35.100
and it makes the world a little bit clearer.

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.270
"Clearer"?

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:39.060
You mean you're doing this for the world?

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:43.350
However things seem in that
broken head of yours, the reality is this:

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:47.720
You've killed many people,
and now I know your true identity.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.970
You fled, but you <i>will </i>be caught, and soon.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:55.470
And when you are, the world really
<i>will </i>improve, by your absence!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:00.970
So, what does this device do?

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.850
Tell me.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.560
How did you find me with this thing?

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:15.970
Of all things, why did the killer
decide to hide inside Kaeru?

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:20.310
And why didn't he escape once hidden?

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:24.640
He could easily have gotten
out when I left the room.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:29.390
He wouldn't even have needed
to open the door or the window.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.720
Oh. Wait a minute...

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:40.180
To him, those gaps don't exist. Is that it?

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:44.720
For him, this disjointed world might be a normal one,

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:47.930
with no gaps and everything connected?

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:52.430
In other words, for him, this <i>is </i>a locked room.

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.970
What about the source of the residents' fear?

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.430
The guy with the cane...

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:02.140
Maybe the killer feared him as well,

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:06.390
so he locked himself in here and was
hiding inside Kaeru's corpse.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:09.520
I see.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.560
Basically, the Perforator's, I mean
Fukuda Tamotsu's, mind is broken into pieces

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.560
and he has no awareness of it.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:19.140
His mind's deceiving him.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.890
Or perhaps it has something to do with

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:25.310
the fairly large piece missing
from Fukuda's frontal lobe...

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:29.930
His worldview assumes
people are broken and in pieces.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:34.180
Perhaps that's precisely why
he drills holes in people's heads.

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:37.810
Then... he's gonna do that to the rookie?

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:41.020
Momoki.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.060
We haven't found Fukuda.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:49.890
But... there is still one way for
Hondomachi to tell us where she is.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.390
Not that it's pleasant to consider.

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.310
I know.

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:56.180
We'll be ready for that.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:18.060
Hondomachi, don't do anything too crazy.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.560
I'll tell you about that device.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:32.520
It's called a Wakumusubi.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:37.100
The well goddess Mizuhanome appears in
the Kojiki, the Nihon Shoki, and the netherworld.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.930
Her son's name is Wakumusubi.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.600
Don't.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.720
Don't just stand there spinning the drill.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.310
You use it...

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.970
...like this!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.770
A new well is forming!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:59.390
Checking field officers' Wakumusubis.

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:00.930
The new well...

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:03.680
...appears to be from Koharu
Hondomachi's Wakumusubi!

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.640
Extract Sakaido!
We're putting him in immediately!

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:09.060
I don't live here!

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:25.220
Narihisago, sorry, but I need
you to dive into a different well.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.470
Understood.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.640
Are you okay?

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.180
Just peachy.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.970
Inject Sakaido.

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.930
I don't know where I am.

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:53.890
Nor do I know what's going on.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:57.220
What I <i>do </i>know...

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.140
...is her name.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.220
Kaeru.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.430
And I'm Sakaido.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.850
I can't remember my full name,

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:12.520
but as the brilliant detective,
I must solve the mystery of her death.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.020
But what <i>is </i>the mystery?

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:30.850
There's no mystery to solve at all.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:34.600
So I guess there's no reason
for me to survive here either.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:40.100
Her legs are bound.
Did she want to look composed?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:41.850
Because she's a girl?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.020
Sakaido is dead.

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:50.850
His time active in the well was 68.25 seconds.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.180
Beginning analysis!

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:54.970
Hondomachi Koharu's face!

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.890
A reflection of it was on the end of the drill.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:01.180
Then there must be other reflections. Find them!

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:05.140
The stainless steel table she's
tied to is made for restaurants.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.390
There's an industrial refrigerator.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:12.220
Extrapolating room size from the angle of
reflection of light from the Wakumusubi.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.270
Between 5.4 and 6.2 meters.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:18.020
There's a closed restaurant three kilometers from Fukuda's house.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.680
Obtaining blueprints.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:23.100
The restaurant's basement
is consistent with the room.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.770
Got that, Mr. Matsuoka?

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.310
Yeah. I'm on my way.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:36.140
It... detects the intent to kill?

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:45.100
It's true. You <i>don't </i>die right away.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.140
Yeah.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:47.520
Thank you.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:49.180
For what?

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:53.560
I drilled holes in all kinds of people.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.850
But that was a mistake.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:59.600
What I really wanted wasn't to
drill a hole in somebody's head.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:03.850
I wanted to see someone
drill the hole themselves.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:06.560
Like you did?

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:10.640
Right. Because I felt I had to.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.180
What's that mean?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.930
How's the breeze?

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.770
Right now... everything is just... cold.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:21.770
Freeze!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:25.930
Step away from there and
get down on the floor, scumbag!

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:28.850
Hondomachi!

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:29.720
She has a pulse!

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.770
She's still alive!

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.970
Don't die, Hondomachi!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:38.770
Come visit me if you pull through!

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:44.430
Fukuda Tamotsu apprehended.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.060
In transit to headquarters.

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:49.060
Got it. Notify me once they arrive.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.060
How's the rookie?

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:53.140
We've heard from the hospital.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.770
Somehow she held on.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.810
Sir?

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.600
There's one more person
to thank for today's success.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:11.930
Good work.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.850
Thank you, sir.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.680
The Perforator was apprehended.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:19.140
Oh, that's great.

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:24.180
This one was a close encounter with John Walker.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:29.140
Yes it was. But he was empty on the inside.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:31.270
What do you think that meant?

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:33.890
It's a product of the human unconscious.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:37.600
There are countless interpretations. For now.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.520
Did you discover any clues about John Walker?

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.720
No.

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:45.520
We got almost nothing.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.310
I could dive again.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:53.850
Yeah. Maybe.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:58.850
I'm fine. It's not my first time dying in the well.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:01.640
But you experience the death, don't you?

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.140
That must take a toll on you.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:08.970
Really? I dunno about that myself.

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:10.810
I'm ready.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:16.560
Is she okay? The girl from your unit.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:20.060
Didn't she have contact with the killer?

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.470
How did you know?

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:26.810
All of a sudden, she acted like she had
gained a mind of her own. Only her.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:32.350
I figured something she did must have
shaken the killer after he targeted her.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:35.720
Yeah. And she suffered for it.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:38.100
But thanks to her, we got the guy.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:43.600
I see. So the second id well today was hers.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:47.560
Impressive. A determined suicide.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:53.770
When I dive into the killer's well again, I bet there will be new elements.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:56.350
I'll look forward to that.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:18:00.970
Every time you dive, you forget
everything and have to start over.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:02.720
That isn't agonizing?

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:06.350
It's part of the fun. You know, to see Kaeru.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.560
It's almost like seeing my daughter.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.020
They're both dead every time.

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.350
Two years, huh.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:18.270
The killer this time...

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:22.270
He knew he and the others were broken,

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:26.100
and yet he didn't realize
his own world was broken.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:29.640
Incredible self-deception, don't you think?

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:32.350
It's hard to understand yourself.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:34.020
Isn't that the issue?

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:37.180
Maybe so.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.680
Are you...

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.140
The killer hid in Kaeru's body...

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.560
He used her corpse...

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.350
That upset you, didn't it?

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.560
Kaeru isn't Muku.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.060
Don't get worked up over
the world of the unconscious.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:57.560
While we're on the subject, remember that you dive to assist the investigation...

00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:00.930
...not to root out the killer's mental weakness.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:03.970
You drove some to suicide.
I don't want a repeat.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.890
A repeat?

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:11.600
Don't you mean a five-peat?

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:13.100
I'm joking.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.180
I'm not going to do that.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:23.930
But if I completely stopped, then wouldn't
I be unable to enter wells anymore?

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:28.270
<i>That </i>would be a problem for both of us.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:40.270
Fukuda Tamotsu makes five--

00:19:40.270 --> 00:19:43.890
five serial killers that appear to
have dealt with John Walker.

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:48.680
But to be able to manipulate people's
unconscious--is that even possible?

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.600
Who can say?

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.770
Kura launched only six months ago.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:20:00.350
But in that short time, you've peered into
a great number of serial killers' wells.

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:03.890
Based on your experience,
what do <i>you </i>think, Mr. Togo?

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:09.430
I doubted John Walker actually existed.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:13.270
I assumed he was a shared
characteristic of serial killers--

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:18.890
something that the Mizuhanome
recorded as a symbol out of convenience.

00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:24.520
Oh. In the same way that Kaeru
always appears and is always dead?

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:29.890
Yes. I thought he was just a default setting
of the wells the Mizuhanome generated.

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:33.350
And that his function wasn't understood yet.

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:39.720
Hmm. At present, I see no
contradictions in that line of thinking.

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:42.850
Besides, even now, no one has elucidated

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:47.310
the entirety of the Mizuhanome's workings.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:51.310
Momoki seems a little
overly concerned with him.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.890
I think it's natural to want to
understand the tools you're using.

00:20:55.890 --> 00:21:00.020
In any case, the residents' reaction
to John Walker's appearance

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:04.560
in the well in this case convinced me.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:07.520
Their fear was unmistakable.

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:12.850
Even though they were completely
unfazed by Kaeru's corpse.

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:16.720
This was not part of the setting of
the world the Mizuhanome generates.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:21.680
I believe it was due to the specific
feelings of the well's owner, the Perforator.

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:26.600
In other words, John Walker actually exists somewhere in this form.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:30.890
Moreover, he implants an impression
so strong it remains in the id.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:35.020
And that has an impact on the impulse to kill.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:39.470
Exactly how one does such a
thing intentionally, I have no idea.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:44.180
Regardless, we are finally forced
to consider the matter in earnest.

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:48.560
To consider an investigation into
John Walker the Serial Killer Creator.

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:41.430
The death you chose was hanging,
not to be run through by a drill.

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:50.770
That's what I should have done.

00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:53.600
For Kaeru's sake.

00:22:53.600 --> 00:22:59.140
Next time I dive into the well, if there's time...

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:02.720
...Sakaido will be able to do that for you.

00:23:02.720 --> 00:23:04.720
As the brilliant detective...

00:23:05.770 --> 00:23:07.310
...he'll know.
